  "extractionNotes": "ZUS notice grants maternity only (217 days at 81.5%) and defers the supplementary and parental parts until discharge and a hospital certificate; no later decision in the file. Those two blocks are in the plan as filed but absent from expected benefits. Weights: one twin 1150 g on two certificates; the other 1280 g on two and 1290 g on two, so it is omitted. Both 28 completed weeks (28+5) and above 1000 g, so the 8-week cap applies. Hospital stays are chains of consecutive certificates from several hospitals (transfers); grouped per child by birth weight and collapsed to one stay each (inferred). The notice confirms both children were still in hospital at its date. Father insured in KRUS; claimant's statement that he will not use parental leave at the same time (dates set to her parental period). Z-3 salary table 2024 (12 months before sick pay from 2025-01-29; carried over to maternity). Column 6 is the contractual amount; contributionBase inferred equal to it. Work-time date on the Z-3 is handwritten and may mark the start of full time. Payer size box not legible."
